guide forever/reputation/cenarion-circle
title Cenarion Circle Reputation
category Reputation
levels 55-60
zone Silithus
# Built from the Era-baseline reference data: Cenarion Hold's Bor Wildmane and
# Huum Wildmane with Secret Communication (8318), Twilight Geolords (8320) and
# the repeatable Encrypted Twilight Texts (8319); the Encrypted Twilight Text
# drop table (Twilight's Hammer cultists, 25% each, Twilight Prophets 100%).
# Farm spots are the densest spawn clusters of the droppers.
#
# The data is the Era (patch 1.12) Silithus, with Cenarion Hold and the Ahn'Qiraj
# war content. Nothing public confirms Forever's Silithus matches it; this has
# NOT been play-tested on Forever yet. Repeatable turn-ins are never flagged
# completed by the client, so those steps track the standing (rep 609). The
# Abyssal Council turn-ins (8361-8364, crests, signets and scepters from
# Templars, Dukes and Lords summoned at the Wind Stones while wearing the
# Twilight Trappings) are in the data but need a summoning setup the data does
# not describe, so they are notes.

step Cenarion Hold
  tip Cenarion Hold is the walled town in north-central Silithus. Bor and Huum Wildmane stand together inside. The Cenarion Circle starts out Neutral. Forever's Legacy Diplomat perk increases reputation gains.
  accept 8318
  accept 8320

step Twilight Base Camp
  tip Twilight's Hammer cultists hold the camps in western Silithus. Twilight Geolords and Stonecallers mix here; any cultist can drop an Encrypted Twilight Text. Every cultist kill also counts toward the Cenarion Circle.
  kill 11881 quest 8320.1 @26.2,33.9
  collect 20404 x10 quest 8318.1 @26.3,32.9

step Back to Cenarion Hold
  turnin 8318
  turnin 8320

step Encrypted Twilight Texts to Friendly
  tip Encrypted Twilight Texts repeats: Bor Wildmane takes more texts again and again. The cultist camps are the place to farm them.
  collect 20404 x10 optional @26.3,32.9
  talk 15306 optional -- Bor Wildmane: Encrypted Twilight Texts (8319)
  rep 609 Friendly

step Cenarion Circle to Honored
  tip Keep farming the Twilight camps. Wearing the Twilight Trappings (the Twilight cultist set plus a Medallion of Station, from Aurel Goldleaf's Medallion of Station quest) lets you summon Abyssal Templars at the Wind Stones; their Abyssal Crests go to Bor Wildmane.
  collect 20404 x10 optional @26.3,32.9
  talk 15306 optional
  rep 609 Honored

step Cenarion Circle to Revered
  tip From here on, the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj raid and the Abyssal Council turn-ins (crests, signets, scepters) carry most of the reputation.
  note Abyssal Crests (8362), Abyssal Signets (8363) and Abyssal Scepters (8364) are repeatable at Bor Wildmane once their opening quests are done.
  rep 609 Revered

step Cenarion Circle to Exalted
  tip Keep running the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and turning in Abyssal Council insignia until Exalted.
  rep 609 Exalted
